    "narrative": "As we look at today\u2019s board for Ghost Ride the WHIP, **Austin Riley** emerges as our strongest play with a 63.46 efficiency score. Despite batting seventh, **Austin Riley** benefits significantly from facing Nick Martinez; the positive park factors and the SP\u2019s manageable xERA of 4.65 provide the cleanest path to production in a day where elite arms are dominating our schedule. **Jose Caballero** remains our secondary priority at 59.76. While his batting order slot is suboptimal, the matchup against Ryan Feltner offers a rare opportunity for stolen bases, with the pitcher\u2019s delivery cadence providing a slight tailwind for **Jose Caballero** to exploit his elite speed\u2014a critical factor for our internal scoring model given our focus on the scarce SB category.\n\nOur most difficult decision involved leaving **Cole Young** on the bench. He finished with a 31.43 score, falling well below our starting threshold due to a brutal matchup against Jacob deGrom. While **Cole Young** possesses the speed upside we crave, the sheer dominance of deGrom\u2019s skill set suppressed his scoring projection far too much to warrant a start. We are also monitoring the potential regression risk for **Josh Naylor** (46.08) and **Isaac Paredes** (49.25), both of whom are essentially fighting for their lives today against deGrom and Wheeler, respectively. Their scores reflect the reality that facing frontline aces essentially nullifies their platoon advantages. With **Corbin Carroll**, **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** all unavailable due to scheduling or rest, we are running thin. We are proceeding with caution, particularly with **Mickey Moniak** (47.82), whose score is tethered to the assumption he makes the lineup, and we are prepared to adjust if the weather or final lineups force a last-minute scramble.",
